# Slice 290: a method writes a name that no binding and no earlier read of the method name, with a name as its tail -- a
# local definition (lm_compiler_local_absent_def), which needs a Structure body.  On the 289 tuple the translation overflowed
# its stack: lm_compiler_declaration asked the head's role, the head was the field this declaration declares, and that role
# asked the same declaration again.  The translation now refuses at the tail.
sub: put_absent (int: v)
    absent_name: v
end: put_absent
int: code 7
put_absent(1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
